硫酯酶活性测定、CRISPR介导的Uba6基因敲除、以及T细胞-肿瘤细胞共培养杀伤实验。对比对象包括野生型与Uba6-null肿瘤细胞、肌苷处理与未处理组、以及不同效靶比下的T细胞杀伤效率。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供人体血浆肌苷水平与生存期关联的临床队列数据，验证肌苷作为ICI疗效生物标志物的价值。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025试验）中，接受纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）治疗的患者基线血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）正相关。高肌苷组的中位OS为33个月，低肌苷组为22个月。该关联仅在ICI治疗组中存在，而在接受mTOR抑制剂依维莫司治疗的对照组中不存在（两组OS无显著差异），表明高肌苷水平特异性地预测ICI疗效。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"数据来源为CheckMate 025临床试验的肾细胞癌患者队列（n=743，其中394人接受纳武利尤单抗，349人接受依维莫司）。分析基于基线血浆代谢组学数据，按各代谢物中位数将患者分为高低两组，使用Cox比例风险模型和Kaplan-Meier曲线评估OS。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R15\\\", \\\"R26\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本文阐述的核心机制是：肌苷作为一种嘌呤代谢物，能够克服肿瘤内在的免疫治疗抵抗。其作用路径并非主要作用于免疫细胞，而是直接靶向肿瘤细胞内的UBA6蛋白。UBA6是一种泛素激活酶，负责激活泛素和泛素样蛋白FAT10。肌苷通过直接结合UBA6，抑制其与E2酶USE1的相互作用及后续的催化活性。UBA6活性的降低解除了对肿瘤细胞内在免疫反应的抑制，导致肿瘤细胞呈现更高的免疫原性，具体表现为MHC-I类分子上调、抗原加工与呈递通路基因表达增加，以及对由CD8+ T细胞分泌的细胞毒性因子（如TNF-α和IFN-γ）更加敏感。这种“热”肿瘤微环境的建立增强了T细胞介导的杀伤作用，从而协同免疫检查点阻断疗法（ICB）提高疗效。临床数据支持这一机制，显示高血浆肌苷水平与接受PD-1抑制剂治疗患者的更长生存期相关。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"肌苷进入肿瘤细胞的具体转运蛋白机制虽提示依赖ENT转运体而非腺苷受体，但具体的分子细节未在正文详细展开。\\\", \\\"虽然建立了肌苷-UBA6-免疫原性的机制，但UBA6下游具体哪些底物的去泛素化或稳定化导致了免疫原性改变，文中指出仍需进一步定义。\\\", \\\"临床验证队列样本量较小（n=22用于UBA6蛋白表达验证），且由于样本缺失，未能同时测量这些患者体内的肌苷水平以进行直接的相关性分析。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n                \"title\": \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\n                \"year\": \"2022\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供肌苷抑制UBA6的具体分子机制证据，包括结合筛选、生化验证及功能回补实验，证明肌苷通过直接靶向肿瘤细胞内的UBA6发挥作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过LiP-SMap化学蛋白质组学筛选，在4T1细胞裂解物中鉴定出23个与肌苷结合的候选蛋白，其中仅UBA6的缺失能显著增强T细胞介导的肿瘤杀伤。体外生化实验证实，肌苷直接减少UBA6与其特异性E2酶USE1之间的相互作用，并降低UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成活性。此外，删除UBA6的泛素折叠结构域（UFD）可消除肌苷对UBA6-USE1相互作用的抑制作用，且UBA6缺失消除了肌苷对T细胞介导肿瘤杀伤的增敏效应，表明肌苷通过直接抑制UBA6活性来增强肿瘤免疫原性。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"使用4T1细胞裂解液进行LiP-SMap筛选；使用HEK293细胞和纯化蛋白进行体外相互作用及硫酯活性测定；使用CRISPR敲除UBA6的4T1和B16-GMCSF肿瘤细胞系进行功能验证。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供血浆肌苷水平与接受ICB治疗患者生存期关联的临床队列数据，确立肌苷作为ICB疗效生物标志物的临床相关性。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在CheckMate 025肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中，接受纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）治疗的患者的血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）呈正相关：高肌苷组中位OS为33个月，低肌苷组为22个月；而在接受依维莫司（mTOR抑制剂）治疗的患者中无此关联。这表明高水平肌苷能为接受ICB治疗的患者带来持久的生存获益。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析CheckMate 025临床试验中394名接受纳武利尤单抗治疗和349名接受依维莫司治疗的RCC患者的血浆代谢谱；以代谢物中位数分组比较OS。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R15\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"补充说明肌苷在肿瘤微环境（TME）中的浓度缺口或来源限制，指出虽然肌苷由肠道菌群产生并可进入循环，但其在TME局部的具体浓度动态及测量受限于腺苷的快速降解，暗示TME内有效肌苷浓度的维持可能存在挑战。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"讨论部分指出，尽管肌苷是腺苷的代谢产物且循环水平受饮食、基因和药物影响，但腺苷在体内可迅速降解为肌苷（约10秒）并在血浆中快速清除（约30秒），而肌苷的生物半衰期较长（约15小时）。由于样本缺失，研究未能在其临床队列中验证肌苷测量或转录组分析。这提示在评估TME中肌苷的实际有效浓度时，需考虑其前体腺苷的不稳定性以及局部摄取机制（如ENT转运体）的作用，目前TME内肌苷的具体浓度缺口及其对UBA6抑制效率的影响尚待进一步解析。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"基于文献综述和讨论部分的逻辑推断，结合研究中提到的腺苷半衰期短、肌苷半衰期长的药代动力学特征，以及未能直接在患者肿瘤组织中测量肌苷的事实。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R55\\\", \\\"R56\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究提出并验证了一个由肌苷调控的UBA6依赖性通路，该通路控制肿瘤的内在免疫原性，进而影响免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的敏感性。核心机制在于：肌苷作为一种嘌呤代谢物，能够直接进入肿瘤细胞（通过ENT转运体而非腺苷受体），并直接结合和抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。UBA6不仅激活泛素，还激活泛素样蛋白FAT10。肌苷通过干扰UBA6与E2酶USE1的结合，抑制了UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成。UBA6活性的降低导致肿瘤细胞内炎症信号通路（如TNF-α、IFN-γ响应基因）和抗原加工/呈递相关基因的上调，从而增加MHC-I表达和肿瘤免疫原性。这种增强的免疫原性使肿瘤细胞对CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性更加敏感，从而克服肿瘤内在的ICB耐药性。临床数据显示，患者血浆中高水平的肌苷以及肿瘤组织中低水平的UBA6表达均与接受ICB治疗后的良好预后（更长的OS/PFS和更高的客观缓解率）相关。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"TME中肌苷的具体局部浓度及其动态变化尚未量化，特别是考虑到腺苷到肌苷的快速转化及清除过程。\\\", \\\"肌苷抑制UBA6后，下游具体的泛素化/FAT10化底物蛋白及其如何具体调控MHC-I上调的详细分子路径仍需进一步阐明。\\\", \\\"不同癌症类型中UBA6表达基线差异对肌苷疗效预测价值的普适性需更大规模队列验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::307f071228c50505d3184f8a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d93294b2fde7fbbbbceb24f3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ee45627bb52c2a851316\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-c0fd2c95dd50ca770222\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-42c295d5bf79b23956eb\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-37c988b582332c2f54a1\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::307f071228c50505d3184f8a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f268dc5a31e6509082426a96\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::915832e3eeeb6c7bf46b4dc7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c9458faeedb93aae1481ce2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究采用多步骤计算与实验结合的策略：1) 利用TCGA bulk RNA-seq数据和ImmuCellAI去卷积算法，鉴定与免疫浸润负相关或正相关的TIIMGs；2) 使用L1000高通量筛选平台，针对TIIMGs筛选739种化合物的转录组扰动效应，并通过drug-to-cell recall验证；3) 在CT26小鼠模型中进行体内给药，收集肿瘤组织进行scRNA-seq，利用NMF算法从肿瘤细胞中提取异质性程序并聚类为12个MPs；4) 开发MP评分算法（结合Cluster 1激活与Cluster 2抑制的加权）量化TME重塑程度；5) 基于MP评分优先选择候选药物（oxypurinol及其前体allopurinol），通过流式细胞术、LC-MS/MS检测肌苷水平、体外共培养及体内协同实验验证机制；6) 回顾性分析人类膀胱癌患者队列中抗痛风药与抗PD-1治疗的生存关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::894b59684f5f72f52dd6cd62\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"建立了首个基于单细胞分辨率的药物诱导TME重塑量化框架（resTMe），定义了12个TME元程序（MPs）和MP评分算法，为预测药物-免疫疗法协同作用提供了新工具。\",\n          \"limits\": \"核心scRNA-seq数据仅来源于小鼠模型（CT26），缺乏人源类器官或PDX模型的直接验证，限制了框架在人类复杂TME中的直接外推性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ef0876af1bde6e00dba83aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"发现了别嘌醇（Allopurinol）作为抗PD-1疗法的潜在增效剂，阐明了其通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性和T细胞功能的分子机制。\",\n          \"limits\": \"机制验证主要在体外细胞系和小鼠模型中进行；人类临床证据仅来自小样本（n=50）、单中心的回顾性观察性研究，存在混杂因素风险，需前瞻性临床试验确认。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b30b08eb075f61505bc09741\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了MDSCs的耗竭是响应性TME的关键标志物，并揭示了低剂量药物可能通过非细胞毒性机制重塑TME以促进免疫浸润。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于其他候选药物（如epirubicin, vemurafenib）的具体分子机制阐述不如AP深入；不同药物对特定免疫亚群的影响差异较大，尚未形成统一的普适性规则。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d89ef3a629b3edc8f1d5680d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"8种癌症类型TCGA数据分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"鉴定出肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），其中COAD拥有最多的dpGenes（792个），KIRC最少，揭示了不同癌症间TME调控网络的异质性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f9f47d7274d6ce123558914d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"L1000平台筛选739种化合物\",\n          \"finding\": \"识别出54种在多癌种中重复出现的候选药物，主要靶向CDKs、HDAC1、PI3K等通路。低剂量处理更倾向于产生非细胞毒性的免疫调节效应，而高剂量常伴随免疫抑制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13b75fe0affb6edd8981d33b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"CT26小鼠模型scRNA-seq分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"药物处理导致肿瘤细胞比例下降，免疫细胞（特别是巨噬细胞、DCs）浸润增加，但MDSCs显著减少。oxypurinol表现出最强的TME重塑能力，显著降低MDSCs并增加抗原呈递相关细胞。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59223824372c97eeae14a917\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"MP评分算法应用\",\n          \"finding\": \"定义了12个MPs，其中Cluster 2（含MPs 1,3,6,8,10,12）与抗原加工和呈递通路高度相关。oxypurinol获得最高MP评分，提示其具有最强的TME重塑潜力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f486a10e036032c79861cfc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Allopurinol (AP) 联合抗PD-1治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"AP通过抑制黄嘌呤脱氢酶（XDH）增加肌苷合成并分泌至胞外，肌苷上调肿瘤细胞MHC I类和PD-L1表达，增强CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性。在CT26模型中，AP联合抗PD-1实现4/6小鼠完全治愈。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5b36a5dbcaf7631b8b07425\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在接受抗PD-1治疗的膀胱癌患者中，同时服用抗痛风药物（如AP或febuxostat）的患者组（n=7）的总生存期（OS）显著优于未服用组（n=43）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a9ba68194211f72c5ff2998\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::309f1460bfa5781083656af4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"如何在复杂的肿瘤微环境中系统性地识别能够增强免疫疗法疗效的药物组合？目前缺乏量化药物诱导TME重塑的系统框架，且难以预测哪些非抗癌药物可作为免疫治疗的增效剂。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::732cd6b3522e68e0af8deae5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究聚焦于实体瘤（以小鼠结肠癌CT26模型和人类膀胱癌队列为主）的肿瘤微环境（TME），探讨药物诱导的TME重塑如何影响免疫检查点抑制剂（如抗PD-1/PD-L1）的疗效。研究对象包括8种癌症类型的TCGA数据、739种免疫调节化合物、小鼠体内的单细胞转录组数据以及临床回顾性队列。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::82ddeb3927993c2d17aa2d61\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的TME重塑的问题。作者首先通过TCGA数据和ImmuCellAI算法鉴定了肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），并利用L1000平台筛选出能显著调控这些基因的化合物。随后，在小鼠CT26肿瘤模型中，通过单细胞RNA测序（scRNA-seq）分析了多种药物处理后的TME变化，识别出12个与TME重塑相关的元程序（Meta-programs, MPs）。基于MP富集情况开发了MP评分算法，用于量化TME对药物的响应程度。该算法成功鉴定出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP），一种痛风药物，发现其能通过促进肌苷（inosine）的合成与分泌，上调肿瘤细胞的MHC I类和PD-L1表达，从而增强CD8+ T细胞的杀伤活性。在体内实验中，低剂量AP联合抗PD-1治疗实现了4/6的小鼠完全肿瘤清除。此外，一项包含50名膀胱癌患者的回顾性研究显示，接受抗痛风药物治疗的患者在抗PD-1治疗下的总生存期显著优于未使用者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29799ff01275a5961dfa4b1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该研究未涉及肠道菌群，因此不能直接回答菌群如何调制ICI疗效的问题，只能作为平行机制或交互作用的潜在背景。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了非微生物来源的代谢物（肌苷）增强ICI疗效的证据。研究发现别嘌醇通过增加肌苷分泌，增强CD8+ T细胞功能，这与某些肠道菌群代谢产物（如丁酸盐、次级胆汁酸）调节免疫微环境的机制形成互补或对比视角。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cc0bd417229ac67f8358b8ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制仅限于别嘌醇-肌苷轴，不能推广为所有ICI增效剂的通用机制。人类证据仅为相关性，因果链条在人体中尚待确证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了别嘌醇增强ICI疗效的具体分子机制：抑制XDH -> 增加肌苷 -> 上调MHC I/PD-L1 -> 增强T细胞杀伤。同时指出MDSCs减少是响应性TME的标志。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ce5af135f0f54a3f33ded5af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"基于小鼠模型数据，人类组织中MDSCs的功能异质性更大，需谨慎外推。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了MDSCs耗竭作为ICI响应生物标志物的实证支持。在scRNA-seq分析中，响应性TME显著特征为MDSCs比例降低。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::911473103290b79cdeaaf990\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"别嘌醇（痛风药）被鉴定为抗PD-1增效剂，并在回顾性临床队列中显示生存获益。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d608d3703ed2d823c7784427\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MP评分算法和12个元程序的定义，量化了抗原呈递、盐应激反应等生物学过程在药物处理后的变化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c11e7ad8dda921d2c87e471\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"AP处理导致肌苷大量分泌，增强OT-I T细胞对B16-OVA肿瘤的杀伤力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a50fe6e4b2c8671f940ffb9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的核心对象是小鼠模型和人类膀胱癌回顾性队列，未直接研究肠道菌群。在将其用于回答‘菌群如何调制ICI’问题时，必须明确其作为‘非菌群代谢机制’的对比或补充角色，而非直接证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78212dc609fe90c3f037d637\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"人类临床数据仅为小样本回顾性观察（n=50），存在选择偏倚和混杂因素，不能作为因果关系的确凿证据，仅能作为假设生成的线索。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::125505f32ce06e79d94ca2a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"别嘌醇的机制特异性强（肌苷轴），不能将其效果泛化为所有代谢调节药物或所有ICI增效剂的共同机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c058dc0771a54f0d89db5a07\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"MP评分和元程序是基于小鼠CT26模型定义的，在不同癌症类型或人源模型中的适用性需进一步验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::50e3812052714d3b820c4e72\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93b0bc69434a90089e6079fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::533541e5da218bf180bf8879\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-c44cb221036f78d05573\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"missing\": [\n                \"jitc-14-3-g001.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g002.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g003.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g004.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g005.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g006.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s001.docx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s002.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s003.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s004.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s005.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s006.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s007.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s008.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s009.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s010.tif\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"graphic_members_unmatched\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementary_bundle_had_no_safe_matching_images\",\n              \"status\": \"unparsed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::514f38127e84ad5c682c0de5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::908d9aeb78769ef90ff4fc57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b8a5a05a2c4c46c244939963\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单中心、随机对照试验设计。纳入符合RECIST v1.1标准的晚期实体瘤患者，按1:1比例随机分组。试验组接受标准免疫治疗联合肌苷（0.2g tid），对照组接受标准免疫治疗。疗效评估每6周进行一次，主要终点为ORR，次要终点为DCR、OS和PFS。使用Kaplan-Meier法计算生存曲线，Cox比例风险模型进行多因素分析，并对不同亚组（如肿瘤类型、炎症指标、转移部位）进行探索性分析以识别潜在受益人群。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::33a5c9e4d60f2557fa054a13\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肌苷联合ICI治疗晚期实体瘤的首个随机对照临床II期数据，证实了肌苷在延长PFS方面的统计学显著性，并为“肠道代谢物调节免疫治疗”假说提供了初步临床支持。\",\n          \"limits\": \"单中心设计导致样本量有限（每组86人）；非盲法设计可能存在偏倚；多肿瘤类型混合导致统计效能分散，OS结果受后续治疗影响较大；亚组分析为探索性，存在多重比较问题，需外部验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::44fd7d0fece39e6e515ee6c0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"全队列（N=172）\",\n          \"finding\": \"肌苷组中位PFS显著长于对照组（7.00 vs 4.40个月，HR=0.63, p=0.011）；ORR为26.7% vs 15.1%（p=0.061，未显著）；中位OS两组无显著差异（HR=1.05, p=0.874）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d691120d6413e21d59a3ebbf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肺癌亚组（N=57）\",\n          \"finding\": \"肌苷组mPFS显著延长（13.80 vs 4.10个月，HR=0.45, p=0.018）；mOS趋势向好但未达显著（HR=0.46, p=0.100）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7efc4f3f1c27bfe2d678132b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"消化道恶性肿瘤亚组（N=55）\",\n          \"finding\": \"肌苷组mPFS有延长趋势但未达显著（5.77 vs 3.50个月，HR=0.63, p=0.121）；mOS无显著差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2dffc3c3672a37974c931734\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"实验室指标亚组（PLR<229, NLR<4, LDH≥216, ENR≤0.012）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在这些特定炎症/代谢标志物背景下，肌苷组PFS均显著优于对照组。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e163eddf36fc1e7cc27c2513\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"安全性评估\",\n          \"finding\": \"肌苷组3-4级不良事件发生率为29%，对照组为36%（p=0.329），提示肌苷可能不增加且略有降低严重不良反应的风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d212be6d9591bb99f87b63b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::326bcdfc7c44333ca4ea1aa5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管临床前研究表明肠道微生物代谢物肌苷可增强ICI疗效，但缺乏人体临床证据。本研究试图解决肌苷作为辅助治疗是否能提高晚期实体瘤患者对PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂的响应率及生存获益的问题。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::96c8a6d462cf5ee52975af40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"单中心、前瞻性、随机、开放标签的II期临床试验。研究对象为晚期恶性实体瘤患者（包括肺癌、消化道肿瘤等），干预措施为在PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂基础上联合口服肌苷（0.2g，每日三次），对照组仅接受PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂±靶向±化疗。主要评估终点为客观缓解率（ORR）、无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1351c9ffeb3960925c4ddd82\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在验证肠道微生物代谢物肌苷能否增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在晚期实体瘤中的疗效。研究在北京友谊医院开展，将172名患者随机分配至肌苷组或对照组。结果显示，与对照组相比，肌苷组显著延长了中位PFS（7.00 vs 4.40个月，HR=0.63, p=0.011），ORR呈上升趋势但未达统计学显著性（26.7% vs 15.1%, p=0.061），OS两组无显著差异。亚组分析显示肌苷在多种基线特征下均能改善PFS。安全性方面，肌苷组3-4级不良反应发生率略低于对照组。结论认为肌苷有潜力增强ICI疗效并降低相关不良反应。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c624786259f743d00b397b1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅在PFS上显示显著优势，ORR和OS未达到统计学显著性；结果受限于单中心和混合肿瘤类型，不能直接外推至所有实体瘤或替代一线标准疗法的地位。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肌苷作为肠道代谢物增强ICI疗效的人体临床数据。具体表现为：在全队列中显著延长PFS（HR=0.63），在肺癌亚组中大幅延长PFS（HR=0.45），并在特定炎症指标（低PLR/NLR，高LDH/ENR）亚组中表现出更显著的PFS获益。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7fc145947c92c1b9b4e13c3f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制部分主要基于作者引用的既往文献（Mager et al., Wang et al., Zhang et al.），本文本身未提供新的机制实验数据（如生物样本分析）。因此，机制解释属于理论支撑，而非本研究的直接发现。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"虽然本文主要报告临床结果，但在背景和讨论中引用并整合了机制研究：肌苷通过抑制UBA6增加肿瘤细胞免疫原性、激活IFN-γ/TNF-α通路、促进CD8+ T细胞增殖、抑制MDSC介导的免疫抑制以及作为CD8+ T细胞的碳源。这些机制解释了为何肌苷能克服ICI耐药。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ad1c1e3f94a45a000796047a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"肌苷的安全性和经济性（已有数十年临床应用历史，用于肝炎辅助治疗），以及其降低3-4级不良反应的趋势（29% vs 36%）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ee3c0ca040f5f7857105c083\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"亚组分析显示，基线炎症指标（PLR, NLR, LDH, ENR）和吸烟/饮酒状态可能与肌苷疗效相关。例如，在非饮酒者、吸烟者、ECOG≥1、无肾上腺/骨/肺转移等亚组中PFS获益更明显。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::330b20611a2b60f0bfb9cb57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是II期单中心研究，样本量较小，OS结果不显著可能受随访时间不足或后续治疗干扰，解读时需谨慎，避免过度推断长期生存获益。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7b8f615eb29b4d96eed30ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"亚组分析多为探索性且未预设校正，显著性结果可能存在假阳性风险，应视为假设生成而非确证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eaa3814986ed246e629fbab5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制描述依赖于文献综述，非本研究实测，需在综述中明确区分临床观察与理论机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::318bfbc9220c4ae9361634f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肌苷效果在不同肿瘤类型间存在异质性（肺癌显著，消化道肿瘤趋势不显著），不能笼统概括为对所有实体瘤均有效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::530b529c34eddfdef2d6f9ae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors cite preclinical mechanisms in the background and discussion, including inosine's role in inhibiting UBA6 to increase tumor immunogenicity, serving as a carbon source for CD8+ T cells, and activating IFN-γ/TNF-α pathways. The study design is a single-center, prospective, randomized, open-label Phase 2 trial registered at ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05809336). The dosage regimen and safety data support the feasibility of repurposing inosine as an adjunct therapy.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-b532f13f7ac0c36c\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-trstv1th\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_23b146d5b5\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"This study does not measure or report the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME) or interstitial fluid. It evaluates the efficacy of administered supplementation rather than correlating baseline endogenous inosine levels with treatment outcomes. Consequently, the specific data regarding natural TME inosine concentrations and their statistical association with ICI efficacy (independent of supplementation) remain unavailable from this material.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study provides clinical evidence that exogenous inosine supplementation (0.2 g, three times/day) combined with PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors significantly prolongs progression-free survival (median 7.00 months vs. 4.40 months; HR 0.63) compared to inhibitors alone in 172 patients with advanced solid tumors. It reports a trend toward improved objective response rate (26.7% vs. 15.1%) and an acceptable safety profile with reduced Grade 3-4 adverse reactions in the inosine group. Subgroup analyses indicate stronger PFS benefits in lung cancer patients and those with specific baseline inflammatory markers (e.g., low PLR/NLR).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::16d078f32ef69dd5a1dca774\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors cite preclinical mechanisms in the background and discussion, including inosine's role in inhibiting UBA6 to increase tumor immunogenicity, serving as a carbon source for CD8+ T cells, and activating IFN-γ/TNF-α pathways. The study design is a single-center, prospective, randomized, open-label Phase 2 trial registered at ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05809336). The dosage regimen and safety data support the feasibility of repurposing inosine as an adjunct therapy.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-b532f13f7ac0c36c\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-trstv1th\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_23b146d5b5\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"This study does not measure or report the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME) or interstitial fluid. It evaluates the efficacy of administered supplementation rather than correlating baseline endogenous inosine levels with treatment outcomes. Consequently, the specific data regarding natural TME inosine concentrations and their statistical association with ICI efficacy (independent of supplementation) remain unavailable from this material.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study provides clinical evidence that exogenous inosine supplementation (0.2 g, three times/day) combined with PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors significantly prolongs progression-free survival (median 7.00 months vs. 4.40 months; HR 0.63) compared to inhibitors alone in 172 patients with advanced solid tumors. It reports a trend toward improved objective response rate (26.7% vs. 15.1%) and an acceptable safety profile with reduced Grade 3-4 adverse reactions in the inosine group. Subgroup analyses indicate stronger PFS benefits in lung cancer patients and those with specific baseline inflammatory markers (e.g., low PLR/NLR).\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ea5b10c585bf0fccd8369c9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0588\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17b5236c305aabb462e37fd0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d47d41f47a3b8d850aa49279\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::797d3a421d1f68362d67ff56\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性机制综述的方法，结合结构化文献检索。检索范围涵盖PubMed/MEDLINE、Embase和Scopus数据库（2010年1月至2026年3月）。筛选标准侧重于具有机制见解和临床应用价值的原创研究、临床试验和高影响力综述。数据提取聚焦于分类特征、生化通路和临床结果，并使用“机制框架分析”将发现归类为系统性免疫调节、局部肿瘤微环境变化和异生物质代谢。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdbb1bb278c9d55b926ad36d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统性地整合了微生物组影响癌症治疗疗效和毒性的多种机制，包括代谢物介导的免疫调节、瘤内微生物群的直接药物相互作用以及性别特异性差异。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为叙述性综述，其证据等级依赖于所选文献的代表性和作者的解释框架；未提供新的原始实验数据或严格的荟萃分析统计结果；不同人群（如东西方）的微生物基线差异可能导致普适性限制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b441a0e563eea1ef2fc56dea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"接受免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的实体瘤患者\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定的细菌组合（如Akkermansia muciniphila、Ruminococcaceae家族成员）及其产生的生物活性代谢物（肌苷、短链脂肪酸、色氨酸衍生物）是ICI成功的关键先决条件；抗生素使用与ICI疗效降低相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2ea197db957bf7d3cfdcc713\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"胰腺癌等实体瘤的微环境\",\n          \"finding\": \"瘤内微生物群（主要是Gammaproteobacteria）表达胞苷脱氨酶（CDA），可将吉西他滨转化为无活性形式，导致化疗耐药；消除这些细菌可恢复药物疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::509a27efd20b1e28804a2fdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"全身免疫系统调节\",\n          \"finding\": \"短链脂肪酸（特别是丁酸盐）作为组蛋白去乙酰化酶抑制剂，增强T细胞适应性；肌苷通过腺苷A2A受体信号通路增强Th1分化，绕过肿瘤微环境的抑制信号。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e9df2e7f615e7f48d48fd7e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"异生物质代谢与毒性\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道细菌产生的β-葡萄糖醛酸酶可重新激活伊立替康，导致严重的黏膜损伤和腹泻；微生物特征可用于预测药物诱导的毒性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4b580cf8eb1d746db1a372d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"造血干细胞移植（HSCT）后\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道微生物多样性丧失是移植相关死亡和移植物抗宿主病（GVHD）的独立风险因素；Blautia属与GVHD相关死亡率降低有关，而肠球菌属扩张加剧炎症。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f209ce7fa8f5c1d829658755\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7550f9285711774c6b8d8c12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"现代肿瘤学正从将肿瘤视为孤立组织块转向将其视为复杂多物种生态系统的一部分。本研究旨在解决的关键问题是：微生物组（特别是肠道和瘤内微生物群）如何调节宿主抗肿瘤免疫，并具体通过哪些机制影响当前化疗和免疫治疗方案的疗效和毒性？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fa09930a8f323cd8b3d7bdfe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肿瘤治疗中的微生物组-宿主轴，涵盖肠道微生物群、瘤内微生物群及其对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效和化疗毒性的影响。研究对象包括成人及儿科实体瘤和血液恶性肿瘤患者，涉及机制模型、临床队列和代谢组学数据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e69c0f1b8396d14a848d7c3e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇叙述性机制综述，旨在全面分析微生物组-宿主轴在癌症治疗中的作用。文章综合了57篇关键文献，探讨了特定细菌群落及其生物活性代谢物（如肌苷、短链脂肪酸、色氨酸衍生物）如何作为免疫检查点抑制剂成功的先决条件。此外，还讨论了细菌酶（如胞苷脱氨酶）在局部药物降解和化疗耐药中的作用，以及新兴的“微生物性别组”在治疗反应和毒性谱中的性别特异性差异。结论强调将微生物监测纳入标准临床协议对于个性化肿瘤治疗和长期生存质量的重要性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4002992b9211ba4203b37df2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要基于综述引用的观察性研究和临床试验结果，具体关联强度因研究而异；未提供统一的量化效应值。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了特定肠道菌群（如Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium pseudolongum）与ICI疗效正相关的证据，以及抗生素使用导致疗效下降的观察结果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3bca396122a57c5c6cb6d384\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述主要来源于体外实验和小鼠模型，部分在人体中的验证程度在所给材料中未完全交代；不同代谢物之间的协同作用细节有限。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了肌苷通过A2A受体信号通路增强Th1分化的机制，以及短链脂肪酸（丁酸盐）通过表观遗传修饰和代谢重编程增强CD8+ T细胞功能的机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e8521b54ac3e1a3aea856bc8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要针对特定类型的化疗药物和特定肿瘤类型（如胰腺癌），其普遍性在其他实体瘤中尚需更多证据支持。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了瘤内微生物群（如胰腺肿瘤中的Gammaproteobacteria）通过表达胞苷脱氨酶（CDA）直接降解化疗药物（吉西他滨）从而导致耐药的机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3968fa9c7bb42ff2c5b57f98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论部分提到儿童癌症幸存者长期存在的菌群改变与代谢综合征、肥胖等并发症的风险增加有关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::49b229ffc3f86574bd68db96\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍“微生物性别组”概念，指出雌激素和雄激素可能通过影响肠道通透性和特定菌群丰度来调节治疗反应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29bc254425f7f72cdf267f30\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"总结了FMT克服ICI原发耐药性的临床试验结果，以及工程菌疗法的前景和风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a9b21bb5521d854910bc6f15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述为叙述性综述，非系统评价或荟萃分析，因此其结论代表了作者的综合性观点而非严格的统计汇总。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47ad2c025201af5d593c97c1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所引用的机制研究多来自小鼠模型或体外实验，其在人体内的直接适用性和效力可能存在差异，需谨慎外推。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c02b5d6501d4c29b43a5f340\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同地理区域和饮食习惯导致的微生物基线差异可能影响某些菌群标志物的普适性，特别是在跨种族比较时。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9162fac3f0939bac1f86cf0b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关于“微生物性别组”的内容较为新兴，具体机制和临床意义仍需更多研究证实，目前主要作为假设提出。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::876aed3948402262e111705c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0124\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b674221023c1dbcd1a299114\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c2620bcc444fc1598dd43ce6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f036c918cd390f5edcdaebe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用还原论视角，从生态水平的菌群相关性分析转向分子水平的机制解析。具体路线包括：1) 梳理建立相关性的大规模测序研究和动物模型实验；2) 验证相关性并识别宿主表型（如CD8+ T细胞浸润）；3) 深入探讨具体的分子机制，分为T细胞刺激、髓系细胞刺激和分子模拟三个子主题；4) 评估基于分子机制的工程化益生菌应用前景。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e6663c1509a79bf070ff83d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统性地从分类学相关性过渡到分子机制，详细列举了多种微生物代谢物和蛋白质如何通过特定受体（GPCRs, A2AR, STING, NOD2, TLR5）和信号通路影响宿主免疫系统。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略和纳入排除标准；主要依赖已发表的小鼠模型和少量临床数据，缺乏大规模前瞻性干预试验的直接证据；对于非细菌类微生物（真菌、古菌）及抑制性微生物的关注不足。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::efc4edd784b59555aab5bd43\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"小鼠模型及患者队列中的相关性研究\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定细菌属（如双歧杆菌、拟杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、普拉梭菌）的存在与ICB疗效正相关，但不同研究间结果存在异质性，且相关性不等于因果性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39351d21f351bf132aaa24af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"粪菌移植（FMT）和单菌定植实验\",\n          \"finding\": \"来自响应者的FMT可重现抗肿瘤效应，增加肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞浸润；特定菌株（如A. muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp.）的单菌定植足以增强ICB疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a2ad8f127a3e2f7fb383b60\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）的作用\",\n          \"finding\": \"SCFAs（如丁酸盐）对ICB的影响具有双重性：通常促进Treg和效应T细胞分化，但在某些情况下（如抗CTLA-4治疗）可能产生负面影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4abe48e8e01b0acc7b17e16a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肌苷（Inosine）通路\",\n          \"finding\": \"B. pseudolongum等产生的肌苷通过结合T细胞上的A2AR受体，协同TLR9激动剂增强抗CTLA-4疗效，但单独使用不足以完全重现表型。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::44f2d548690b4b10bf73e2c7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Akkermansia muciniphila与STING通路\",\n          \"finding\": \"A. muciniphila产生cdAMP，激活STING信号，诱导I型干扰素产生，招募NK细胞和树突状细胞，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e7fda87890cf100670bbed03\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Enterococcus sagA蛋白与NOD2通路\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠球菌表达的SagA蛋白降解肽聚糖产生muropeptides，激活宿主NOD2受体，促进炎症环境和CD8+ T细胞浸润。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a33dc878424e5c612918cf2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"分子模拟机制\",\n          \"finding\": \"E. hirae中的噬菌体尾长测量蛋白（TMP）含有与宿主PSMB4蛋白相似的表位，引发交叉反应性CD8+ T细胞，增强抗PD-1疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::41b69dd74275e596257e7f30\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ecae2ad21b9875306feb272\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知特定微生物群与ICB疗效相关，但确切的分子机制尚不清楚，这限制了将微生物作为精准医疗手段加以利用的能力。本文试图回答：哪些具体的微生物分子特征（蛋白质、酶、代谢物）介导了这种调节作用？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::68dac395c061b642520773c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"人类微生物群（特别是肠道菌群）与癌症免疫治疗中免疫检查点阻断（ICB，如抗PD-1/PD-L1和抗CTLA-4抗体）疗效之间的关系。研究范围涵盖从宏观的菌群组成相关性到微观的分子机制（代谢物、蛋白质、抗原模拟），以及基于这些机制的工程化益生菌策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c8095064895dfad406e569df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在总结宿主-微生物相互作用在检查点抑制剂免疫治疗背景下的分子理解进展。文章首先回顾了通过小鼠模型和患者队列建立的菌群与ICB疗效之间的相关性，指出仅凭分类学关联难以确定因果关系。随后，重点阐述了具体的微生物分子机制，包括短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、肌苷（inosine）、环二腺苷酸（cdAMP）、肽聚糖片段（muropeptides）和鞭毛蛋白（flagellin）如何分别通过T细胞刺激、髓系细胞激活或分子模拟来增强抗肿瘤免疫。最后，讨论了利用这些分子特征设计下一代工程化益生菌以改善治疗反应的潜力，并指出了当前研究在真菌/古菌、抑制性微生物及远端器官微生物方面的局限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::599e6bf17709ba8cfbd90929\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些机制大多基于小鼠模型或体外实验，部分已在早期临床试验中探索（如MRx0518），但尚未成为标准治疗指南；不同菌株间存在显著差异，不能简单外推至所有同种细菌。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICB疗效的具体生物学途径和关键分子中介。例如，明确了A. muciniphila通过cdAMP-STING轴、肠球菌通过SagA-NOD2轴、以及双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR轴增强抗肿瘤免疫的具体机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a57617739887231108e77d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制的复杂性在于多种微生物可能通过相同或不同的路径产生相似效果（冗余性），且单一代谢物往往不足以完全重现体内复杂的生态效应（如肌苷需配合TLR9激动剂）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细描述了介导效应的具体分子机制，包括代谢物（SCFAs, inosine, cdAMP）、蛋白质（SagA, flagellin）和抗原模拟（TMP）。解释了这些分子如何被宿主受体识别并触发下游信号级联反应（如I型干扰素产生、Th1分化、CD8+ T细胞浸润）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4eb4f4671e999f3795550859\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出目前大多数研究集中在细菌，而忽略了真菌、古菌以及具有免疫抑制作用的负相关微生物；同时提到了远端器官（如肿瘤内部）微生物群的潜在作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07f07877dcebdfd835240f4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"对比了生态方法（FMT、饮食调整、定义菌群）与还原论方法（小分子、工程化益生菌）的优缺点。指出前者面临标准化和个体差异挑战，后者更具精准性但开发难度大。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3730e786b8b2831b6d7fa00a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的许多机制（如cdAMP, SagA）主要在小鼠模型中验证，其在人体内的确切效力和安全性仍需更多临床数据支持。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e90d9bb4a7244676654bef0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者强调“还原论”方法的优势，但这并不意味着生态方法无效，两者应被视为互补而非对立。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3abfe02af60077a50b3004b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同菌株甚至同一物种的不同菌株之间可能存在巨大的功能差异（如Bifidobacterium bifidum的不同菌株对PD-1阻断的影响不同），因此在引用具体机制时需严格限定菌株来源。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0d593217581a78566b8d13de\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"SCFAs（特别是丁酸盐）对ICB的影响具有情境依赖性（如对CTLA-4可能有负面作用），不能一概而论地认为其总是有益。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::54d4ead502cd94815f6b6dba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9cb666a107fc8e343e94fb0e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cca7c1de9f7fc15ee3968e02\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::972e64916e571eefa7631020\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究采用多步骤实验设计：首先，使用六种临床相关抗生素处理C57BL/6J小鼠，建立不同的肠道菌群和代谢组状态，并结合ICT治疗评估肿瘤生长；其次，利用液相色谱-质谱联用技术（LC-MS）对粪便、血清和肿瘤组织进行非靶向代谢组学 profiling，筛选与肿瘤负荷相关的代谢物，并通过靶向定量验证候选分子（TDCA）；再次，通过体内回补实验测试不同胆汁酸对抗生素诱导的ICT低响应的挽救作用；接着，利用单细胞RNA测序（scRNA-seq）、流式细胞术和多因子蛋白检测分析肿瘤微环境中免疫细胞亚群的变化；最后，通过抗体耗竭实验确定关键效应细胞，并利用OT-I转基因小鼠模型和TGR5拮抗剂（SBI-115）在体外和体内验证TDCA通过TGR5受体直接增强CD8+ T细胞细胞毒性的机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::04d1653e627f38a25eb88134\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"识别出微生物衍生的胆汁酸TDCA是连接抗生素诱导的菌群紊乱与ICT低响应的关键代谢介质。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代TDCA在人体内的确切药代动力学特征及长期安全性数据；机制研究主要在预临床小鼠模型中进行，人类相关性主要基于之前的回顾性临床关联数据，缺乏前瞻性患者验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e73cb7c8039043ab17f7ea02\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证明了单一微生物代谢物的补充即可逆转抗生素引起的免疫治疗失效，无需重建整个微生物组。\",\n          \"limits\": \"未明确驱动TDCA丧失的具体微生物类群和酶促途径；TGR5的作用可能涉及其他细胞类型，本研究主要依赖药理学拮抗剂而非基因敲除，无法完全排除脱靶效应或其他细胞类型的贡献。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a8acea12fabd6b703f06ba14\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了TDCA通过TGR5受体直接增强CD8+ T细胞细胞毒性的新机制，区别于其他代谢物对T细胞分化的间接调节。\",\n          \"limits\": \"TDCA对CD8+ T细胞下游的具体信号转导通路（如cAMP-PKA-mTOR）尚未完全阐明；TDCA的疗效可能具有肿瘤类型、免疫背景和剂量依赖性，其在其他实体瘤中的普适性需进一步验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7fea3693f3c5f89fd8b539c0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"C57BL/6J小鼠接种B16-F10黑色素瘤细胞，接受青霉素/链霉素（Pen/Strep）等抗生素处理及ICT治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"Pen/Strep处理显著减少肠道细菌总量并改变菌群结构，导致肿瘤体积增大和生存期缩短，表明抗生素特异性地降低了ICT的疗效而非直接影响肿瘤 intrinsic 生长。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8437e3e49f9c6298637b1691\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"非靶向代谢组学分析与临床数据交叉验证\",\n          \"finding\": \"抗生素处理重塑了宿主代谢组，其中牛磺脱氧胆酸（TDCA）在肿瘤、血清和盲肠内容物中呈现一致的变化趋势，且在人类黑色素瘤ICT响应者中富集，被鉴定为ICT响应的关键代谢物。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a5fd9f87fca22b5def42a90\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Pen/Strep处理后靶向定量肿瘤内胆汁酸\",\n          \"finding\": \"抗生素处理导致肿瘤内初级结合胆汁酸（如TCDCA）增加，而微生物衍生的次级胆汁酸TDCA显著耗竭。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3ce8b9357b67d5a78510ea79\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在抗生素+ICT背景下，向肿瘤内局部注射五种受抗生素影响的胆汁酸\",\n          \"finding\": \"仅TDCA补充能显著抑制肿瘤生长并延长生存期，且仅在抗生素存在时发挥挽救作用，不影响无抗生素背景下的ICT疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d4be51fd1e5e2dbe963267ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在E0771乳腺癌模型和人源化NSG-SGM3小鼠A375黑色素瘤模型中补充TDCA\",\n          \"finding\": \"TDCA补充在多种肿瘤模型中均能克服抗生素诱导的ICT低响应，显示其效应的广泛性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c795da1eca5470b6d5a3d608\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"单细胞RNA测序与流式细胞术分析肿瘤浸润免疫细胞\",\n          \"finding\": \"TDCA处理增加了肿瘤内效应CD8+ T细胞、γδ T细胞和NK细胞的比例，减少了耗竭型CD8+ T细胞，并提高了IFN-γ、TNF-α和颗粒酶B等效应细胞因子的水平。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f703234a9a62db92de4c7264\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"CD4+ T细胞、CD8+ T细胞或NK细胞特异性耗竭实验\",\n          \"finding\": \"CD8+ T细胞的完全耗竭消除了TDCA的抗肿瘤效应，证明CD8+ T细胞是TDCA介导肿瘤控制的主要效应细胞。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f500276a42430cc5a45e0812\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"OT-I转基因小鼠CD8+ T细胞体外杀伤实验及过继转移\",\n          \"finding\": \"TDCA直接增强抗原特异性CD8+ T细胞的细胞毒性，促进靶细胞死亡；过继转移经TDCA处理的CD8+ T细胞可延缓肿瘤生长。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c862a9f0e53059cee0615b43\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TGR5/FXR/VDR报告基因 assay 及体内TGR5拮抗剂（SBI-115）干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"TDCA主要激活TGR5受体；药理学阻断TGR5可抵消TDCA对肿瘤生长的控制和CD8+ T细胞的效应功能，证实TDCA通过TGR5信号通路发挥作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fed6a02f4d94d96a258ecee9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8711e939876d048b7fecf9e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"抗生素诱导的肠道菌群紊乱如何具体导致免疫检查点疗法（ICT）的低响应？是否存在特定的微生物衍生代谢物能够介导这一过程，并可通过补充该代谢物来逆转抗生素引起的免疫治疗失效？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5890e6775c83a71dc398f9a5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究以小鼠黑色素瘤（B16-F10）、乳腺癌（E0771）及人源化小鼠黑色素瘤模型为研究对象，聚焦于抗生素干扰肠道菌群后对免疫检查点疗法（ICT）疗效的影响。研究范围涵盖多种临床常用抗生素的扰动效应、肿瘤微环境中的代谢组学变化、CD8+ T细胞的免疫反应机制以及特定微生物代谢物（TDCA）的替代治疗潜力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::772b8bb0a0da67855f9d96c9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在解决抗生素使用导致癌症患者对免疫检查点疗法（ICT）低响应这一临床难题，探究其背后的微生物介导机制。作者通过联合应用多株抗生素扰动小鼠模型与非靶向代谢组学分析，识别出微生物衍生的次级胆汁酸牛磺脱氧胆酸（TDCA）作为ICT响应的关键决定因子。研究发现，抗生素（特别是青霉素/链霉素）显著降低肿瘤内TDCA水平，而外源性补充TDCA足以克服抗生素引起的ICT低响应，并在多种肿瘤模型中恢复抗肿瘤免疫。机制上，TDCA不直接作用于肿瘤细胞，而是通过结合TGR5受体，直接增强CD8+ T细胞的效应功能和细胞毒性。这项工作确立了“微生物代谢物-TGR5-CD8+ T细胞”轴在维持ICT疗效中的作用，并提出代谢物替代疗法作为缓解抗生素相关免疫治疗失效的策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b486452b9ed92fdf3585969b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要基于小鼠模型，且针对的是特定抗生素组合和黑色素瘤/乳腺癌模型，不同抗生素种类和肿瘤类型的效果可能存在差异。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了抗生素干扰肠道菌群导致ICT疗效下降的具体代谢机制：抗生素（如Pen/Strep）导致微生物衍生的次级胆汁酸TDCA在肿瘤内耗竭，从而削弱抗肿瘤免疫。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b164cce26337f952c15d4f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制验证依赖于TGR5药理学拮抗剂，未排除其他潜在受体或细胞类型的作用；下游信号通路细节尚不明确。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了TDCA通过直接结合TGR5受体，增强CD8+ T细胞的效应功能和细胞毒性，从而恢复ICT疗效的分子机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::511c6539987cda5f95a9cca8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"目前仅为概念验证，缺乏人体临床试验数据支持；需考虑代谢物的给药途径、剂量及稳定性问题。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了‘代谢物替代疗法’作为克服抗生素相关ICT低响应的潜在策略，证明了补充单一代谢物TDCA即可恢复疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0576011fdd7240f5fca0ecb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中讨论了其他胆汁酸（如DCA、UDCA）在不同肿瘤背景下对免疫的不同影响（抑制或促进），以及其它代谢物（如肌醇、短链脂肪酸）的作用机制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::107a3be4bd8567f3889b635f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中指出不同抗生素对菌群和代谢组的扰动程度不同，导致ICT响应差异，这解释了为何临床研究中抗生素对免疫治疗的影响不一致。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7d029ff36f9ec29b337e4298\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论部分指出代谢物替代避免了活菌疗法的定植困难、安全性和监管复杂性等问题。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::870daf920ef09f8d06d5dd8d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的机制结论主要基于小鼠模型，虽然引用了之前的人类队列数据作为关联支持，但TDCA在人体内的确切疗效和安全性尚未在本研究中得到前瞻性验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cd327c27a8ebee5fd1f368a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"TDCA的作用依赖于TGR5受体，但其下游信号通路（如cAMP-PKA-mTOR）的具体运作机制在本研究中仅为推测，需结合后续研究谨慎解读。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c333cd1be808b2bc7d897b03\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同胆汁酸在不同肿瘤类型中具有相反的免疫调节作用（如DCA在结直肠癌中抑制免疫，而在本研究中TDCA在黑色素瘤中促进免疫），因此在跨肿瘤类型推广时需特别注意上下文差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd7fef3939ea77630336d1de\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"抗生素对ICT的影响并非均一，不同抗生素导致的菌群和代谢组变化不同，因此不能简单地将所有抗生素视为同等负面因素。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8cf778affe1781ab11c7d82a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0481\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-8c71e871c7aa5482d545\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f85da31c482f020fe5f7\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7a6e9bd3a48b1fef12e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-12c6cac6a4bef2539d08\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-02faf8b9fedd6313c05e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-3aa25875e4222837763e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::845f1f0f9faa43750eb0252c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e029480226395ee65355068\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a150faa5f38ad58aa803aa87\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 队列构建：前瞻性招募uHCC患者，严格排除近期使用抗生素、益生菌等干扰因素者。分为训练集（OR vs PD，n=20 vs 21）和验证集（n=33）。 2. 样本处理：收集治疗前新鲜粪便，-80°C保存。 3. 微生物组分析：提取DNA，扩增16S rRNA V3-V4区，Illumina MiSeq测序。使用QIIME进行OTU聚类，SILVA数据库注释。计算Alpha多样性（Shannon, PD whole tree），Beta多样性（PCoA, Bray-Curtis, PERMANOVA）。使用LEfSe鉴定差异菌属。 4. 代谢物分析：LC-MS检测39种胆汁酸，HPLC检测短链脂肪酸。 5. 统计分析：相关性分析（Spearman）关联菌群与代谢物。ROC曲线确定最佳截断值。Kaplan-Meier法和Log-rank检验评估生存差异。Cox比例风险模型进行多变量生存分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f3ad86f29db4aec656ccb78\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"首次在包含验证队列的HCC研究中，确立了基线肠道微生物组（特别是Lachnoclostridium/Prevotella 9平衡）和次级胆汁酸（UDCA/UCA）与ICI治疗疗效及生存期的关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"观察性研究，无法确立因果关系；机制需体外实验验证；主要基于病毒相关HCC，外推至非病毒性HCC需谨慎；未涵盖当前一线标准疗法（阿替利珠单抗+贝伐珠单抗）；缺乏动态监测和免疫微环境（如PBMC）数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::205a3810c4b95c603021af2d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"训练集（OR vs PD）\",\n          \"finding\": \"OR患者粪便中Lachnoclostridium、Lachnospiraceae和Veillonella富集；PD患者中Prevotella 9富集。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17127989af6f9015ee06d3c1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"训练集（OR vs PD）\",\n          \"finding\": \"OR患者粪便中次级胆汁酸（UDCA, UCA, MDCA）显著高于PD患者；SCFA无显著差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0658b769e832eb1ea64e6389\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"相关性分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"UDCA、UCA、MDCA的浓度与Lachnoclostridium丰度呈正相关，与Prevotella 9丰度呈负相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::81de4c9543a29d42bda91fff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"生存分析（训练集）\",\n          \"finding\": \"Lachnoclostridium高丰度且Prevotella 9低丰度的“良好”微生物特征组合显著预测更好的总生存期（OS）。在多变量Cox模型中，该特征仍是OS的独立预测因子。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0d88cc9ec2296d5ef9927be6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"验证集\",\n          \"finding\": \"具有“良好”微生物特征的患者表现出更长的无进展生存期（PFS: 8.8 vs 1.8个月）和总生存期（OS: 未达vs 6.5个月，p<0.001）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ece6acafa06099b8b6423101\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::60020e34ec4b8c77e0d8f810\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"目前缺乏有效的生物标志物来预测uHCC患者对ICI治疗的反应。尽管有证据表明肠道微生物群可能调节肿瘤对免疫治疗的反应，但在HCC中的具体作用尚不明确。本研究试图回答：uHCC患者的基线肠道微生物组和代谢物是否与ICI治疗结局相关？能否识别出预测生存期的微生物特征？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0201844e7f6258c10ee9924c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不可切除肝细胞癌（uHCC）患者，接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；比较客观缓解（OR）、疾病进展（PD）及健康对照者的粪便微生物组与代谢物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15e6a333c649c99338c34cf2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探索肠道微生物群及其代谢产物作为预测uHCC患者ICI治疗疗效的生物标志物的潜力。研究采用前瞻性队列设计，在2018年5月至2020年2月期间，纳入94名初治uHCC患者，收集治疗前粪便样本。通过16S rRNA基因测序分析微生物组成，并通过LC-MS和HPLC分析胆汁酸（BA）和短链脂肪酸（SCFA）。训练集包含20例OR患者和21例PD患者，验证集为33例Child-Pugh A级患者。研究发现，基线时OR与PD患者的肠道菌群存在显著差异，特定菌属丰度及次级胆汁酸水平与治疗效果相关，且特定的微生物特征组合可独立预测总生存期（OS）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::326b44aebea94784d1e576bd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限于uHCC人群；主要基于抗PD-1/PD-L1单药或联合TKI治疗，未直接验证阿替利珠单抗+贝伐珠单抗方案；关联性强于因果性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的微生物特征（Lachnoclostridium富集 + Prevotella 9耗竭）与uHCC患者ICI治疗客观缓解率（ORR）和无进展生存期（PFS）的正向关联证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::83aec2be22646133caa52f92\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"相关性而非因果性；机制假设（Clostridium scindens的作用）未被本实验直接证实，仅引用文献支持；未测量免疫细胞浸润或细胞因子水平以直接验证免疫调节机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定细菌（Lachnoclostridium）与特定代谢物（次级胆汁酸UDCA/UCA）之间的强正相关性，并指出这些胆汁酸在响应者中富集。作者推测Lachnoclostridium可能通过转化CDCA生成具有化学预防作用的UDCA来介导效应。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::85a98285bb070f39fc5b770b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"引言部分回顾了HCC流行病学、ICI治疗现状（响应率16-20%）、现有生物标志物（PD-L1, CTNNB1, AFP）的局限性，以及肠道微生物群在其他癌症（黑色素瘤）中调节免疫治疗效果的已有证据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9891353d147403f3d76c46ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"详细的16S rRNA测序流程、代谢物提取与分析方法、统计模型（LEfSe, Cox回归）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b157a758206c4af9a002c10c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的发现主要基于台湾地区的病毒相关HCC患者，可能不适用于非病毒性HCC或其他种族群体。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8540bbaebe850fd2e0ab6a37\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"验证队列规模较小（n=33），且主要为Child-Pugh A级，限制了其在晚期肝病人群中的普适性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e0f143e6499a564f8b9b8c38\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究未区分ICI单药与联合治疗（如ICI+TKI）对微生物组的潜在不同影响，尽管分析显示既往TKI暴露未显著混淆结果，但联合治疗本身可能改变肠道环境。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a0bee8c0a20e76b35b352b7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“首次包含验证队列”需注意其语境，即针对HCC ICI治疗这一特定细分领域，而非整个微生物组领域。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bde1cd61b2336480314a8bed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a28d5e97bd70ca15780b288\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::44e2883db3f80d2e4ff54fcb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2b1327a2e56c81674bf43a74\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 临床观察基础：引用BEWEL试验，确立BRB饮食富集毛螺菌科与增强ICI疗效的关联。 2. 体内功能验证：在C57BL/6小鼠异种移植模型（MC38细胞）中，分别单独补充三种毛螺菌科菌株（B. obeum, B. massiliensis, A. rectalis），并与IgG对照组及抗PD-1治疗组比较，评估其对ICI抗肿瘤活性的影响。 3. 比较基因组学分析：提取这三种菌株的全基因组序列，使用KEGGREST映射和clusterProfiler进行过度代表测试，以所有基因组编码的KO为背景，识别B. obeum和B. massiliensis共有但A. rectalis缺失的177个KEGG正交ologs。 4. 通路注释与机制推断：将识别出的独特KO映射到KEGG通路，重点分析与免疫代谢相关的四类通路（乙酸产生、维生素合成、细胞壁修饰、胆汁酸转化），以此推断潜在的生物学机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7f6c2dda0eed5148ca99cf62\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的因果证据链：从临床饮食干预（BRB）到特定菌群富集，再到单一菌株的功能验证（B. obeum/massiliensis有效 vs A. rectalis无效），最后通过比较基因组学锁定潜在机制基因集。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的肿瘤抑制率数据、统计学显著性水平、菌株定植效率验证细节、以及体内代谢物（如乙酸、维生素、胆汁酸）的实际浓度测量结果。机制推断主要基于基因组存在性，而非直接的代谢产物功能验证或宿主免疫细胞表型的直接检测。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::49075a4aa403451e95cfd0e7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在小鼠异种移植模型中，单独补充B. obeum或B. massiliensis，联合抗PD-1治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"显著改善了ICI的抗肿瘤有效性\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d890857321a53b0ea271e5dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在小鼠异种移植模型中，单独补充A. rectalis，联合抗PD-1治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"未观察到对ICI有效性的改善\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e07affb6db39f836d72263d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"比较B. obeum, B. massiliensis与A. rectalis的基因组\",\n          \"finding\": \"鉴定出177个仅在有效菌株（B. obeum, B. massiliensis）中存在而在无效菌株（A. rectalis）中缺失的KEGG正交ologs\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::52462292839e9c73194026ae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对这177个独特KO进行KEGG通路富集分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"发现四个关键通路：(1) Wood-Ljungdahl途径基因（产乙酸，T细胞能量来源）；(2) 叶酸(B9)和钴胺素(B12)合成基因（支持T细胞增殖）；(3) L-鼠李糖合成基因（细胞壁装饰，激活先天免疫）；(4) 胆汁酸转化为次级异构胆汁酸的基因（调节FXR/TGR5受体，影响Th17/Treg平衡）\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b0923f43402a3ad6c97f803\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7247ccac03a0e89f056f79d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，且BRB饮食能富集毛螺菌科并增强疗效，但具体是哪些毛螺菌科菌株起作用，以及它们通过何种分子机制介导这种疗效增强？特别是为何某些菌株有效而其他近缘菌株无效？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::16c32a22f7ba956f404fab1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n  